            <div class="prose max-w-none" x-show="lang === 'en'" x-cloak>
                <h2>Background</h2>
<p>Overseas advertising platforms (Meta, Google, TikTok, etc.) rely heavily on account balance management for campaign stability. Insufficient account balance leading to ad pauses can disrupt daily conversion metrics at best and derail entire campaign strategies at worst. This SOP aims to help operations teams establish standardized fund management processes to ensure account balances remain sufficient, recharge approvals are compliant, and reconciliation is clear and traceable.</p>
<hr />
<h2>SOP 1: Daily Balance Inspection (Required Daily)</h2>
<h3>Timing</h3>
<p>Complete before 9:00 AM each business day; adjust to 8:00 AM during holiday seasons or major promotion periods.</p>
<h3>Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Log into Ad Management Dashboard</strong></li>
<li>Open each platform's account list (Meta Business Manager / Google Ads / TikTok Ads Center)</li>
<li>
<p>Verify current account balance and daily spend projection</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Calculate Days of Coverage</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Formula: Days of Coverage = Current Balance ÷ Average Daily Spend (Yesterday)</li>
<li>If days &lt; 2: Mark as "Urgent Recharge"</li>
<li>
<p>If days &lt; 5: Mark as "Warning Recharge"</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Complete Inspection Report</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Record each account's balance, spend velocity, and status</li>
<li>Sync to finance reconciliation group (WeCom/Feishu)</li>
</ol>
<h3>Common Issues</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Cross-timezone Spend Variance</strong>: TikTok US market peak hours are EST 6-11 PM, corresponding to Beijing time 7 AM-12 PM next day; balance inspections should account for timezone differences</li>
<li><strong>Cache Delays</strong>: Some platforms show balance with 15-30 minute delays; actual platform charge records should be used as reference</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>SOP 2: Recharge Application and Approval</h2>
<h3>Trigger Conditions</h3>
<ul>
<li>Days of coverage &lt; 5 days</li>
<li>Single recharge &gt; USD 5,000 equivalent</li>
<li>First recharge for new accounts</li>
</ul>
<h3>Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Submit Recharge Application</strong></li>
<li>Complete "Ad Account Recharge Application Form": account name, platform, recharge amount, currency, projected spend cycle</li>
<li>
<p>Attach: inspection report screenshot + spend trend screenshot</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Finance Initial Review</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Verify application amount matches account historical spend</li>
<li>
<p>Confirm account ownership (self-operated/agency/channel)</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Operations Manager Review</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Confirm recharge priority</li>
<li>
<p>Large recharges (single transaction &gt; USD 20,000) require additional ROI projection documentation</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Execute Recharge</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Use enterprise payment channels (PayPal Business Account / Wire Transfer / Platform Direct Connect)</li>
<li>
<p>Retain recharge receipt screenshot</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Archive Records</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Update ledgers within 24 hours of recharge completion</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>SOP 3: Multi-Account Fund Allocation</h2>
<h3>Applicable Scenarios</h3>
<p>When unified fund management is needed across multiple accounts, or when an account experiences sudden high spend requiring emergency allocation.</p>
<h3>Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Assess Donor Account Safety Margin</strong></li>
<li>Donor account must have &gt; 7 days of coverage</li>
<li>
<p>Confirm no pending large recharges for donor account</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Calculate Allocation Amount</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Reference recipient account's 7-day average daily spend × target coverage days (recommend 10-14 days)</li>
<li>
<p>Avoid over-allocation that creates funding pressure on donor account</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Execute Transfer</strong></p>
</li>
<li>If platform supports, use sub-account transfers (e.g., Meta Business Platform)</li>
<li>
<p>If cross-account transfers aren't supported, record as "accounts receivable" and prioritize future recharge for that account</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Notify Stakeholders</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Sync with operations + finance after transfer completion, both parties confirm</li>
</ol>
<h3>Notes</h3>
<ul>
<li>Some platforms (e.g., Google Ads) don't support cross-account balance sharing; individual recharges required</li>
<li>Agency account transfers require additional client written confirmation</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>SOP 4: Financial Reconciliation and Monthly Audit</h2>
<h3>Reconciliation Schedule</h3>
<p>Weekly reconciliation every Friday; monthly reconciliation on the last business day of each month.</p>
<h3>Reconciliation Steps</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Export Platform Invoices</strong></li>
<li>Meta: Reports → Billing → Download CSV</li>
<li>Google Ads: Tools → Billing → Documents</li>
<li>
<p>TikTok Ads: Finance → Billing History</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Compare with Ledger</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Items to verify: recharge amount, spend amount, refund amount, account balance</li>
<li>Variance rate = |Platform Invoice - Ledger Record| ÷ Ledger Record</li>
<li>
<p>Variance rate &gt; 1% requires investigation</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Variance Investigation</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Common causes: timezone settlement differences, platform fees, currency exchange losses, delayed refunds</li>
<li>
<p>Document variance causes for record</p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Generate Reconciliation Report</strong></p>
</li>
<li>Weekly report: account balance and spend summary</li>
<li>Monthly report: overall spend trends, recharge cost analysis, optimization recommendations</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>SOP 5: Abnormal Risk Control Monitoring</h2>
<h3>Metrics and Thresholds</h3>
<table>
<thead>
<tr>
<th>Metric</th>
<th>Warning Threshold</th>
<th>Action</th>
</tr>
</thead>
<tbody>
<tr>
<td>Hourly spend spike</td>
<td>&gt; 3× daily average</td>
<td>Immediately pause ad set; investigate potential creative bugs or click fraud</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Days of coverage</td>
<td>&lt; 2 days</td>
<td>Trigger emergency recharge process</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Recharge delay</td>
<td>&gt; 2 hours past platform promise</td>
<td>Contact platform support + verify payment status with finance</td>
</tr>
<tr>
<td>Negative balance</td>
<td>Any occurrence</td>
<td>Immediately stop campaigns; investigate potential click fraud</td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
<h3>Exception Handling Process</h3>
<ol>
<li>Detect anomaly → Screenshot for evidence</li>
<li>Pause related ads (operations has autonomous authority)</li>
<li>Report to direct supervisor within 15 minutes</li>
<li>Issue preliminary analysis report within 2 hours</li>
<li>If financial loss involved, submit complete incident report to finance + legal within 24 hours</li>
</ol>
<hr />
<h2>Quick Reference: Key Metrics</h2>
<p>Operations staff may use these metrics as core references for daily inspections:</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Days of Coverage</strong>: Reflects fund sufficiency; target ≥ 7 days</li>
<li><strong>Average Daily Spend</strong>: Measures campaign scale for recharge budget planning</li>
<li><strong>Recharge Frequency</strong>: High frequency indicates insufficient fund planning; low frequency may miss campaign opportunities</li>
<li><strong>Reconciliation Variance Rate</strong>: Target &lt; 1%; reflects ledger accuracy</li>
<li><strong>Abnormal Spend Incidents</strong>: Important risk control metric during monthly reviews</li>
</ul>
<hr />
<h2>Conclusion</h2>
<p>The core of overseas advertising fund management isn't "recharging more" but "precise control, proactive warning, and rapid response." Establishing standardized SOPs enables operations teams to maintain healthy fund chain operations even when facing complex multi-account, high-spend scenarios. If your team hasn't yet established complete fund management ledgers, start with SOP 1 (Daily Balance Inspection) and progressively build out subsequent processes.</p>
